data: {"type":"toolResult","tool_result":{"call":{"provider":"call_k8saPtV12l0Jb7f8W4fgxrCf"},"name":"search_world","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nightjar (ship, courier ship) [ID: b0cd3a42-d5b0-44dd-972d-da7d960aab40]: A courier ship captained by Asha Pell. It carries blue salt from Orin to Vesper between April and September; winter ice closes the strait.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a1873c-dda9-7bf5-a8c5-094ae62ee4c8\n  - â CAPTAINS from Asha Pell (person) [ID: 731a80b4-1cd1-40e2-9fe7-618d14dd3932] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Born on Orin, Asha Pell moved to Vesper at age six and grew up there. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She keeps a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - â NAVIGATES from Iven Marr (person) [ID: 05ff3f16-a6a5-4f4c-833b-8f226a7a345d]: Asha Pell's navigator on the Nightjar; the only person who knows she has the small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates using tide charts, not magic.\n  - TRANSPORTS â Blue salt (mineral, fuel) [ID: 8f0beecf-61cb-4419-99eb-e2030a4eafb7]: A salt mined on the island of Orin that powers the lenses of Vesper's tidal lighthouse.\n\nAsha Pell (person) [ID: 731a80b4-1cd1-40e2-9fe7-618d14dd3932] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Born on Orin, Asha Pell moved to Vesper at age six and grew up there. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She keeps a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  Properties: additional_source_conversation: 01a1873c-dda9-7bf5-a8c5-094ae62ee4c8; source_conversation: 01a1873c-dda9-7bf5-a8c5-094ae62ee4c8\n  - â NAVIGATES_FOR from Iven Marr (person) [ID: 05ff3f16-a6a5-4f4c-833b-8f226a7a345d]: Asha Pell's navigator on the Nightjar; the only person who knows she has the small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates using tide charts, not magic.\n  - CAPTAINS â Nightjar (ship, courier ship) [ID: b0cd3a42-d5b0-44dd-972d-da7d960aab40]: A courier ship captained by Asha Pell. It carries blue salt from Orin to Vesper between April and September; winter ice closes the strait.\n  - GREW_UP_IN â Vesper (city, port) [ID: 8e5eb323-f581-4ce1-8cf4-8bceb6847598]: Brinewake's main port city, built around a tidal lighthouse.\n  - MEMBER_OF â Lantern Guild (guild) [ID: 8ada2504-3940-4fa0-9142-7b15d6e2c8fa]: The guild that maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners; it does not own the mines. When the strait freezes in winter, the guild uses stored blue salt.\n  - CONCEALS â Asha's small brass key (key, object) [ID: 085fe1cd-e389-4552-bce4-9349fb8600f4]: A small brass key sewn inside Asha Pell's left coat cuff; it opens the old lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse.\n  - TRUSTS_WITH â Iven Marr (person) [ID: 05ff3f16-a6a5-4f4c-833b-8f226a7a345d]: Asha Pell's navigator on the Nightjar; the only person who knows she has the small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates using tide charts, not magic.\n  - DOES_NOT_ALLOW_TO_NEGOTIATE â Iven Marr (person) [ID: 05ff3f16-a6a5-4f4c-833b-8f226a7a345d]: Asha Pell's navigator on the Nightjar; the only person who knows she has the small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. He lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates using tide charts, not magic.\n  - BORN_IN â Orin (island) [ID: 9bac8802-f464-491c-b86e-9c90ec862af2]: An island where blue salt is mined.\n\nOld lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse (room, location) [ID: 287f4345-79ad-4e32-9acc-6168a9aafe18]: An old lens room beneath Vesper's tidal lighthouse, opened by Asha Pell's small brass key. A rockfall permanently sealed it in 318. Nobody has reopened it, and it has no other entrance.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a1873c-dda9-7bf5-a8c5-094ae62ee4c8\n  - â OPENS from Asha's small brass key (key, object) [ID: 085fe1cd-e389-4552-bce4-9349fb8600f4]: A small brass key sewn inside Asha Pell's left coat cuff; it opens the old lens room beneath Vesper's lighthouse.\n  - LOCATED_BENEATH â Tidal lighthouse of Vesper (lighthouse) [ID: 76dc2022-8211-4657-b177-03c04d118558]: A tidal lighthouse around which Vesper is built. Its lenses run on blue salt.\n\nLantern Guild (guild) [ID: 8ada2504-3940-4fa0-9142-7b15d6e2c8fa]: The guild that maintains Vesper's tidal lighthouse and buys blue salt from Orin's miners; it does not own the mines. When the strait freezes in winter, the guild uses stored blue salt.\n  - â MEMBER_OF from Asha Pell (person) [ID: 731a80b4-1cd1-40e2-9fe7-618d14dd3932] [Aliases: Captain Ash]: Born on Orin, Asha Pell moved to Vesper at age six and grew up there. She captains the courier ship Nightjar and belongs to the Lantern Guild; her crew usually calls her Captain Ash. She keeps a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff; only her navigator, Iven Marr, knows she has it.\n  - â HONORS_CIVILIAN_CONTRACTS_WITH from Sera Dain (person) [ID: 4e7f03b3-a66c-4627-9e62-3e2ba6943d5c]: Leader of the Deep Bell Union. She refuses to sell salt to the military but continues to honor civilian contracts with the Lantern Guild.\n  - â REFUSES_TO_JOIN from Bren Vale (person) [ID: 9a340887-524b-4387-9b69-d7e321c84b3a] [Aliases: Captain]: Captain of the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild; he refuses to join because he distrusts Tal Ren's friends.\n  - MAINTAINS â Tidal lighthouse of Vesper (lighthouse) [ID: 76dc2022-8211-4657-b177-03c04d118558]: A tidal lighthouse around which Vesper is built. Its lenses run on blue salt.\n  - BUYS_FROM â Orin's miners (worker group) [ID: 92474181-bc9f-4dc2-bf64-51e67969f1ea]: Miners on Orin who mine blue salt; the Lantern Guild buys salt from them. They formed the Deep Bell Union.\n  - USES_STORED â Blue salt (mineral, fuel) [ID: 8f0beecf-61cb-4419-99eb-e2030a4eafb7]: A salt mined on the island of Orin that powers the lenses of Vesper's tidal lighthouse.\n  - OPPOSES â Toll on blue salt shipments (toll, policy) [ID: 2521192a-96cc-4cd6-849e-31b02c7d959e]: A toll on blue salt shipments imposed in 319 by Vesper's governor, Tal Ren. The Lantern Guild opposes it. Bren Vale supports it because the revenue repairs fishing piers.\n\nPetrel (ship, fishing boat) [ID: 0d21b413-13c7-4726-8b6b-c8f12484a752]: A fishing boat captained by Bren Vale.\n  Properties: source_conversation: 01a1873c-dda9-7bf5-a8c5-094ae62ee4c8\n  - â CAPTAINS from Bren Vale (person) [ID: 9a340887-524b-4387-9b69-d7e321c84b3a] [Aliases: Captain]: Captain of the fishing boat Petrel. People on the dock call him Captain. He is unrelated to Asha Pell and is not a member of the Lantern Guild; he refuses to join because he distrusts Tal Ren's friends.\n  - â COOKS_ABOARD from Nessa (person) [ID: f66f3aa9-5f75-441b-9921-530cd348de93]: The Petrel's cook and Bren Vale's older sister. She is not his employee on a formal wage.\n  - â ABOARD from Button (animal, cat) [ID: bff96558-5e46-4181-8b98-665de1d66329]: A black cat kept by Nessa aboard the Petrel."}]}}

